A||||16||mrfixit58||Power Steering Possibilities||||3||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||02-17-2000||05:29 PM||||I was reading the other day and found mention that the later MR2 models came from the factory with power steering. Since they have the same drivetrain configuration, has anyone looked into adapting their system to a Fiero? Has anyone ever seen an MR2 with power steering?||||reg||3
Z||000001||TOM||02-17-2000||09:31 PM||||Why use cheap jap parts when you can adapt gm parts easier and why with the lightness these have in the front end?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||02-18-2000||02:45 AM||||If you have an 88, the mounts for power steering are already one the front end bits.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||02-18-2000||09:06 AM||||I figured I would get a little greef for mentioning the MR2 on this site. I only brought this up based on what I learned.<P>Tom... I'm not aware that there is other GM "stuff" that can be adapted. Can you expound on this?<P>Roy L.||||reg||12
Z||000004||Phil||02-18-2000||09:49 AM||||Just my 2 cents but what would you gain with power steering on these cars? I don't find the steering effort even when parked to be difficult. To me it is akin to spending $500 for a 1HP gain, not worth the $ or the bother.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||02-18-2000||12:53 PM||||I imagine there are power steering racks that might fit the Fiero.  The problem I see is where do you put the pump?  Pontiac was about to release an electric power steering option when the project was killed.  I've read that a few even made it out of the factory with the option installed.<P>I agree that power steering is not a problem for me but my wife and daughters would surely appreciate it.  My middle daughter has an 86 RX/7 with power steering.  The steering is very quick and easy.  It also has a much shorter turning radius than the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||02-18-2000||01:15 PM||||According to my sources (which are usually reliable), there were 13 '88 Fieros with p/s from the factory (probably sitting in the back of some execs garage) and another 100 units built for aftermarket sale.  Who knows where the aftermarket units are now?  Maybe in some GM warehouse collecting dust.  My guess is that someone forgot about them.  Maybe if someone could get a part #, one of us could scope it out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spyder||02-18-2000||01:16 PM||||When you add stabilizer bars front and rear you don’t need the  steering dampener anymore. The shock on the steering.  Once removed you don’t notice it not being power.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shiner||02-18-2000||02:01 PM||||The steering effort went WAY up whent I went from my '84 SC to my '87 GT.  The quicker steering ratio on the GT and the fat tires really made parking manuevers take a bit more muscle.  It doesn't bother me one bit, but for smaller people with GT's, I could see it bieng a pain.  But once you get it moving even the SMALLEST bit, the steering lightens up.  And once I started driving fieros, other cars seemed so dead feeling!  You really get the sensation of a tie rod in each hand!  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||02-18-2000||03:11 PM||||Shiner,<P>I agree. Once the car is moving there is no problem. My wife is five foot-nothing and drove an 85 GT for several years with no problem. <P>Carrolles,<P>If I remember correctly, the MR2 has electric steering just like the 88 Fiero was supposed to have. <P>If anyone happens on a repair manual for the MR2, take a quick look at the steering section and see if they do, indeed, have power steering.<P>Roy<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fiero56||02-18-2000||03:18 PM||||Rodney Dickman has one of the original power steering systems. I don't remember the exact story, but he found one, and I've heard he put it on his Mera. I haven't actually asked him if he installed it, but people have told me he did.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||02-18-2000||03:38 PM||||You can buy either the standard or sport steering rack from Autozone for $114 plus a $50 core charge.  It might help if you go with the lighter rack.  Surely it would be a bunch cheaper.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierosound||02-18-2000||07:47 PM||||Every few weeks someone asks the same question - how do I get power steering on my FIERO? - without ever checking the previous posts...  There IS a power steering kit available SPECIFICALLY for the FIERO.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001828.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001828.html</A> <P><BR>Cliff...<P>As new members sign onto the forums, it may be a good idea to send them a message acquainting them with some of the Forum's features - particularly the SEARCH function. Thanks.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Monkeyman||02-18-2000||11:24 PM||||The "search" button could be a little larger, but anyone who doesn't see it is just being a little lazy.  (Don't get on me--I've had the same problem)  That or they have a 4" monitor.||||reg||1
Z||000014||mrfixit58||02-19-2000||06:07 PM||||fierosound, Monkeyman,<P>Thank-you for mentioning the earlier post on the power steering conversion. However, if you'll note the topic of my ORIGINAL post, you'll see that I was mentioning the conversion possibilities of the ELECTRIC MR2 unit. <P>Although I was aware of the conversion kit you mentioned, others who replied to this thread may not have been. I, also, am not interested in paying someone $1300 for a conversion kit if I could make one myself with junk yard parts. I only mentioned it to see if anyone else had seen the MR2 PS unit and thought about the same thing as me.<P>Thanks for posting the previous thread but, please, becareful about name calling... it can only lead to negitive feelings.<P>Roy L.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Phil||02-19-2000||06:27 PM||||Actually it's kind of nice seeing the same questions again because now I've gotten the answers from all you people. I then can be the first to give the correct answer to a new member and they are very impressed with this super brillant Phil guy. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||07:02 PM||||mrfixit58--The only name calling I did was to call some people (including myself) lazy for not looking around for the search button.  Nothing personal was intended.||||reg||1
